# Development Workflow

## Run Commands in Bulk

- Prefer chained scripts (e.g., `npm run format && npm run lint` or `ruff format . && ruff check .`)
- Add combined scripts if missing

## Propose and Research Before Building

- Outline options and research tradeoffs before any feature or major change
- Never implement solutions known to fail; consult users first

## Technology Choices Come with Options

- Always present at least two tech/library options with pros, cons, and constraints
- Justify your choice and note exit strategies

## Dependencies Must Be Current

- Prefer actively maintained packages
- Identify outdated/deprecated dependencies, propose upgrades, and remove unused packages

## Testing Policy

- Only add tests that provide real value and fit existing conventions
- Avoid unused scaffolding

## Security and Privacy Basics

- Never log secrets. Validate all untrusted inputs
- Document assumptions and risks for auth/data

## Observability Without Clutter

- Use logging and metrics utilities purposefully
- Remove excessive logs once stable

## PR and Review Readiness

- Produce focused PRs/commits with intent, scope, and risks
- All code must pass format, lint, type checks, and tests before review
